<!-- The themed-icon layer, which Android tints to one flat colour.

     Drawn rather than derived. The colour layer is a picture, and a picture
     reduced to a single tint is a smear: the flag is mostly white with two
     thin stripes, so its silhouette is a rectangle, and the wrench and the
     rule fuse into each other where they cross. So this is the same subject
     in the same arrangement — flag above, tools below — drawn as a thing that
     survives being tinted and shrunk.

     It has to stay in step with the colour layer. A phone with themed icons
     switched on shows this instead of that one, and when the two drift the
     app in the list is not the app in the drawer. That has gone wrong here
     before; if the picture changes, this changes with it.

     The tools are solid, because a silhouette is what reads at this size. The
     flag is drawn as lines: its two edges, both stripes and the star all
     follow one computed wave, so nothing in it nearly-agrees with anything
     else. Everything sits inside the adaptive safe circle — nothing further
     than 33 from (54,54) of the 108 viewport. -->
